                <pb facs="0203" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg91"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 23700/36.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Beaupré.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-06-13"><hi rendition="#italic">June 13,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department instructs Mr. Beaupré to withdraw application for extradition of
                    Knepper, as department is informed by the governor of Illinois that no further
                    steps will be taken to secure fugitive’s extradition.</p>
            </div>
